
Why Java 8 Came:
Before Java 8, Java code was often:

lengthy
repetitive
more boilerplate
slower to write
harder to process collections/data cleanly

Example: simple tasks like sorting, filtering, looping needed many lines of code.

So Java 8 came to make Java:
shorter to write
easier to read
faster for data processing
modern like newer languages
better for multi-core processors

Why It Is Important
Because Java 8 introduced features used
in almost every modern Java project:

Main Important Features:
Lambda expressions → short code
Stream API → filter/map/sort data easily
Functional interfaces
Optional → avoid null issues
New Date/Time API → better than old Date class
In One Line
Java 8 came to modernize Java and reduce unnecessary code
-----------------------------------------------------
What is Lambda Expression?
A lambda expression is a short way to write implementation of a method
Lambda expression was introduced to reduce boilerplate code, replace anonymous inner classes,
 and support functional programming in Java.